# MOA-2008-BLG-379: the resolved lens minus the source, Keck-II NIRC2
# narrow camera, Ks (Bennett et al. 2024, AJ 168, 15, the table "Keck
# NIRC2 Narrow Camera Fit Parameters": its two epoch rows "2018 May" and
# "2018 Aug", not the weighted sum; star 1 = lens, star 2 = source, as
# identified with the 2013 Hubble images in their Hubble section).
#
# Columns: time [BJD_TDB]  dE [mas]  dN [mas]  err_E [mas]  err_N [mas]  corr
#   dE = RA_1 - RA_2 (true arc), dN = DEC_1 - DEC_2.
#   time: the paper gives only the UT dates (2018 May 26, 2018 Aug 6); the
#   rows are placed at 12:00 UT, mid-night at Maunakea.  Half a day is
#   0.008 mas of motion at 5.76 mas/yr, far below the errors.
#   corr: not published; 0.
